# J11 — "What can this thing do?"
# Persona: returning user who forgot the verbs. help → tools/modules →
# ghost-text. Known risk: 67 flat tools + dead ghost-text = discoverability
# wall.
name: Discoverability — what can this thing do
env: KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1 KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING=1
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
wait-for: 30 KUZUSHI
submit: help
wait: 2
snap: help
ask: `help` — is it grouped by operator task (scan/triage/export/...) or an alphabetical wall? Could a returning user find their next verb in <10s?
keys: Escape
submit: help planner
wait: 2
snap: help-phase-shortcuts
expect: open the Map phase planner
expect: open the Scan phase planner
expect: open the Review phase planner
expect: open the Prove phase planner
expect: open the Fix phase planner
ask: Phase shortcuts: are `/map`, `/scan`, `/review`, `/prove`, and `/fix` presented as direct planning surfaces rather than pipeline launchers?
keys: Escape
submit: help full
wait: 2
snap: help-full-pipeline
expect: full [target]
expect: hand off to Review or Report
expect: /pipeline [target]
ask: Guided workflow: is `/full [target]` clearly the guided Map → Scan workflow and Review/Report handoff, with `/pipeline [target]` discoverable as its alias?
keys: Escape
submit: tools
wait: 2
snap: tools
ask: `tools` — 67-flat-tools wall check: is the list navigable (grouped, searchable, paged) or a scroll dump?
submit: modules
wait: 2
snap: modules
ask: `modules` — do module rows say what each is FOR, and does the catalog point at `use <module>` as the next step?
keys: Escape
wait: 1
type: sc
wait: 1
snap: ghost-text
ask: Ghost-text — with a partial verb typed ("sc"), does completion/ghost-text offer anything, or is it dead (July finding)?
keys: Escape
